:: Waking Troubles 2 [event mom_quest] {"position":"3025,950","size":"100,100"}
<<silently>>
<<SetLocation "Bedroom">>
<<CheckLocation>>
<</silently>>

The door clicks shut behind us. $mom.callName moves a hoodie off the edge of my bed, folds it without thinking, and sits down. I sit next to her. On the desk the prototype is already waiting, and while she's busy looking disappointed at a plate I forgot to bring downstairs, I reach over and switch it on. <<UseQuestDevice $mom>>

<<Video "images/characters/player/prototype/on.mp4" "" "" 500>>

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Thanks for coming up. I didn't really want to talk about this in the hallway." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Of course, honey. You look a little worn out. Is it the company?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Sort of. It's mostly the mornings. I wake up and my head's already going a hundred miles an hour about clients and bugs and money, and by the time I actually get out of bed I'm tired again." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Oh, I know that feeling, it's like the day starts without you and you spend the rest of it trying to catch up." },
{ who: $player, text: "And the alarm doesn't help. It goes off and it's like someone's yelling at me." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She pats my knee twice, the way she used to when I was sick and pretending I wasn't. The prototype hums along on the desk, quieter than the fan in my laptop. I can see her turning it over, and I try very hard not to look like I'm waiting for anything.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "What if I woke you up? Gently, I mean, a knock and a 'good morning' instead of that alarm screaming at you." },
{ who: $player, text: "You'd do that? You've got your own mornings, $mom.callName. I don't want to be one more thing on your list." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Oh, please, you're not a thing on a list, and I'm up at six anyway. I could even bring you a coffee. Black with just a little milk, right?" },
{ who: $player, text: "You remember how I take it?" },
{ who: $mom, text: "Honey, I've been making you coffee since you were old enough to steal mine." },
{ who: $player, text: "Okay. Yeah. If you're really offering, that would honestly help a lot." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Then it's settled. What time, seven?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Seven thirty? Seven feels a little cruel." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Seven thirty it is. I'll set my alarm a bit earlier and have it ready, and if you're about to ask for breakfast in bed too, don't push your luck." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She laughs at her own joke, and I lean in and hug her. She hugs back the way she always does, both arms, a little too tight, her chin on my shoulder. She's warm and soft against me, and she smells like her perfume and the coffee she had this afternoon. When she starts to pull back, I don't, and after a moment she settles in again. She doesn't seem to mind.

When she finally lets go, she's already reaching for her phone.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Right, I really have to call Karen back before she files a missing person report. <<if $time.current.value == 0>>See you at breakfast?<<elseif $time.current.value == 4>>Dinner's in an hour, okay?<<else>>And don't stay up too late, okay?<</if>>" },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She leaves the door open a crack on her way out, and a moment later I hear her work voice start up again down the hall. I switch the prototype off. Coffee in bed every morning at a time I picked, and she walked out of here thinking it was her idea. It's such a small thing that I feel a little silly for being this pleased, but it's the first part of her day I've put there myself.
/*<<set $mom.flags.wakeUp = true>>*/
<<ProfileLog $mom "Slow and Steady" "She offered to wake me up every morning at seven thirty, with a cup of coffee, the way I like it.">>
<<NextQuest $mom>>
<<ReturnFromEvent>>


